5. The compiled script of the KCC20 contract inside the recorded transactions of the
   testnet runs.

   A Kaspa transaction that spends a coin of a contract reveals the contract's script. Of
   the 9 transactions kept in each of

     testnet/results/2026-10-15-testnet-10/chain.json
     testnet/results/2026-10-30-testnet-10/chain.json

   the 8 that spend a token coin (all but the first) therefore carry, in the signature
   script of that input, the compiled script of the contract KCC20 of the KCC20 reference
   (see 1) whole: after the state fields of the coin, byte for byte the rest of the bytecode in
   that repository's fixtures/public-mint/artifact.json, revision c8a0871. The 4 of them in each
   file that were accepted were accepted by Kaspa testnet-10 nodes on the day of that record
   and were public there; the explorer's answers for those 4 in the explorer/ folder of the
   same record carry it too. The 4 refused transactions are kept beside them. The one
   transaction of

     testnet/results/2026-10-30-testnet-10/collect/collect-tx.json

   spends three token coins and carries it in each of its three inputs; it was accepted on
   2026-10-30 and was public there, and the explorer's answer for it, explorer/C1.json in the
   same record, carries it too. No other file of this repository carries it, and no script
   of the other two contracts of the reference is carried.

